      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-09-30_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <p>BRITISH WORKERS' NATIONAL LEAGUE GREAT PATRIOTIC MEETING. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), OCTOBER Ist, in THE ROYAL COURT THEATRE, at 7.30 p.m. Speakers: Mr. JOSEPH TERRETT (London), Mr. J. A. SEDDON (St. Helens). Chairman: JAMES SEXTON, Esq. Come and hear what our men are doing at the Front!</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON CORPORATION OAS DEPARTMENT. .</p>
        <p>At the urgent request of the Government the Gas Committee have consented to extract more Spirit from the Gas.</p>
        <p>-Cc;iis-u-IWO—rs---a--re---ii-dvised to REPLACE ALL PLAT FLAME BURNERS BY INCAN- DESCENT LIGHTS, which will be much more economical. _ _</p>
        <p>W. S. HADDOCK, General Manager. Gag Offices, Mersey-street, September 7th, 1916.</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE MICHAELMAS QUARTER SESSIONS.</p>
        <p>„NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the (JiENERAL QUARTER SESSIONS OF THE PEACE for the County of Lancaster will be hOlden at the Castle of LANCASTER, on MONDAY, the 16th day of October, 1916, at eleven o'clock in the forenoon; and by adjourn- rnent at the following places and times, viz. the Court House, in PRESTON, on ,WEIjNESDAY, the 19th day of October, 1916, at t'ellt o'clock in the forenoon.</p>
        <p>At- the Assize Courts. in MANCHESTER, on A,IONDAY, the 23rd day of October, 1916, at 4alf-past ten o'clock in the forenoon. • ,At the County Sessions House, in LIVER- rOOL, on TUESDAY, .the 31st day of October, 1916, at half-past ten o'clock in the forenoon. The Solicitors engaged in Prosecutions at the said Sessions are requested to take notice that 411 Depositions and Instructions for indictments re required to be sent to the Clerk of the _ "Ws Office seven days at least before the said sehsions respectively. ' HARCOURT E. CLARE. • - Clerk of the Peace. Clerk of the Peace's Office, Preston, September 29th, 191 g.</p>
        <p>DERBY . WAR WARRINGTON</p>
