      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-09-30_WidnesExaminer_art0113" n="art0113">
        <head>PRIVATE H. BRAZENDALE.</head>
        <p>PRIVATE H. BRAZENDALE.</p>
        <p>Fine Tributes From Officers</p>
        <p>And Men.</p>
        <p>Mr. and Mrs. T. W. Brazendale, 26, Thelwall- lane, have been informed of the death in Action of their son, Private Herbert Brazendale, of the South Lancs. Regiment.</p>
        <p>An officer, writing on September 16th, said: "These are just a few lines written on behalf of myself and the officers of B Company, to express to you our sorrow in the death of your son, and our sympathy with you in your grief. Liked both by officers and men, he was a good soldier and is a great loss to the company. I trust that it will be some consolation to you to know that he died doing his duty." A comrade, Lance-Corporal J. Clarke, wrctte</p>
