      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-09-30_WidnesExaminer_art0200" n="art0200">
        <head>LING.</head>
        <p>LING.</p>
        <p>THREE-ASIDE GAMES.,</p>
        <p>Works Association Competition</p>
        <p>Concluded.</p>
        <p>The postponed three-aside bowling competition in connection with the Warrington Works Amateur Association was brought to a conclusion on the Arp- ley green on Saturday. Beautiful weather condi- tions prevailed, and the sport was of the best. The final game between Mr. T: Mannering's team (No. 1) and Mr- H. Whitley's team resulted in a draw, following which a deciding game of five up was played, Mr, liannering's team winning by 15 points to 8.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-09-30_WidnesExaminer_art0201" n="art0201">
        <head>AN OFFICIALS' MAIN.</head>
        <p>AN OFFICIALS' MAIN.</p>
        <p>The Works Association bowling season concludes to-day. with an officials' main at the Cat and Lion, Stretton.</p>
        <p>KING AND QUEEN ,CLUIR.</p>
        <p>President's Alain Held On Saturday.</p>
        <p>Ideal weather favoured the above main, held on Saturday. There were forty entries, and some fine sport was witnessed. Most of the games were very evenly contested, with the exception of the final, which proved" a very one-sided affair, Ball being very fortunate to \ escape a clean plate." The results are appended:— Preliminary Round. . 15 Langley .. . 15 W. Locker ... 15 W. Holloway ... 15 A. Holloway ... 15 S. Leigh .... .... 15 F. Faulkes . ... 15 S. Garnett .. First Round. . 15 J. Kaye .... .15 E. Povey . 15 J. Monks . . 15 E. Rowlands . 15 3. Mborfield</p>
