        <head>STRETTON PUBLICAN</head>
        <p>STRETTON PUBLICAN</p>
        <p>• Fails To Report And Is Handed Ove,r: On Wednesday, at a Special Court held Stockton Heath, John Starkey, licensee of tr. Cat and and Lion Inn, Stretton, was charged - s fore Messrs. T. Baxter and C. Jackson 110110 with having failed to report himself t 02.0.. military authorities, as required by the wAlfst tary Service Act. Defendant is in his fortrw-</p>
        <p>year. th° Acting=Sergeant Worth, who preferred charge, gave evidence as to carrying out structions received from the military auth°red Defendant said that he had not rece,ind, any papers -requiring that he should atLe—ly He was quite willing to go up and was °Jibe waiting for the papers. He admitted that had not made any inquiry on the subject,. „rt Captain Luck, Chester Castle, told the u°"t, that the papers had been posted to defendanns but, owing to a clerical error, his name It', wrongly spelled and the documents‘ had o°l back through the dead letter department. Aid Under the circumstances the magistrates "._ not impose any fine, but ordered defendant to be handed oter to the military escort.</p>
