        <p>PRIVATE .11. SMART. Third Brother Who Has Been Wounded. Private Harold Sinart, South Lancs. Regi- ment, son of Mr. Smart, confectioner, 32, Queen-street, has been wounded. This is the third and youngest of Mr. Smart's sons to he wounded. Private Smart is progressing as well as can be expected. He is 22 years of age, and</p>
        <p>hind they will get one of our rifles and fire cn us as soon as we turn our backs." Rifleman Howard, who is nineteen years of age, joined the Army in August, 1914, and went to the Front in May last year. He was wounded the following August, and after four; months in an, English hospital, he went back in November. He was educated at the Wycliffe and Beamont Schools, and was formerly employed by McDowells, motor builders. He belonged to the Ist Warrington Troop Boy Scouts, and formerly attended Orford Sunday School. - PRIVATE J. WAKEFIELD. Gassed In June Last Year; Nov Wounded. Mr. and Mrs. Wakefield; 30, Queen-street, hai.;.e been informed that their son, Private Joseph</p>
