        <p>J. Craddock . 15 W Leigh E. Bothwell H. Langhorn ... 15 T. S. Steel R. Savory ..... . 15 H. GatleY W. Ball , 15 F. Hambleton ...... 13 J. Barnard G. Clifford J. Smith T. Carter • 15 F. Clare H. Wilde J. Watkins ... ...... . 15 E. Balmer Second Round. J. Watkins ......... 15 J. Warburton W. Ball R. Savory W. Johnstone W. Bridge T. Carter G. Clifford G. Jones Third Round. T. Carter W. Johnstone W. Ball G. Jones Semi-Final. W. Ball W. Johnstone s l5 G. Jones ..... 11 Final. W. Johnstone CLOSING MAIN. Secretary Wins First Prize At The • Liberal Club. The Liberal Club held their closing main on Saturday, when nearly fifty- members took part. This is a record for these times. There was some good bowling, although the green was slightly damp, and the interest the members took was high. Many thanks are due to the gentlemen who gave the prizes. The successful members were as follow: 1, George Marshall (hon. secretary); 2, Frank Stir- lingileet; 3, T. Drew; 4, John Collins; 5. Frank Plurapton; 6, William Daintith; 7, Thomas Dutton: 8, •John Graham. The prizes will be distributed by Alderman D. Tinnion on the general meeting night in October. LIBERAL CI.US v. CALEDONIAN ASSOCIATION. The Liberal Club play the ret-arn match.'with the Caledonian Association on the Cemetery Bowling Green to-day. BANK QUAY CHARITY The seCond round in the Bank Quay Charity Main was completed on Saturday, the following being the winners:— J. Hands (3) 13-12, W. White (4) 13-8, S. Taylor, (3), 13-11, B. Jennings (3) 13-12. A. Webb (4) 13-12, E. Hill (C.) (5) 13-5, T. Whittaker (3) 13-5, W. Webb (4) 13-10, R. Graham (4) 13-41, T. Sutcliffe (4) 13-12,-J. Pritchard (5) 14-10, J. E. Thomasson (3) 13-7, C. Smith (4) 13-9, .f. 'Massey (3) 13-7, T. Amos (4) 13-10, J. Bird (4) 13-12, J. Joyner (5) 13-11, A. Broadhurst l;.;••.', 13-5, J. Wltson (3) 13-12, A. Mulhill ;4) 11 -If:. John Appletlon (scr.) 13-6, R. Harrison (4) 13-5, H. Massey (4) 13-10. T. Jackson (M. 11. (4) 13-11. J. Watts (3) 13-10, J